  "goodToKnow": "Der Besatzer is an occupier, often with a negative tone; the neutral term is die Besatzungsmacht (occupying power). After 1945, Germany was divided into American, British, French and Soviet Besatzungszonen. Die Besatzung also means a ship's or plane's crew. Besetzen means to occupy, and besetzt means taken or engaged. The plural is the same."
